    "details": "Wasmtime development team reports:\n\n> - Out-of-bounds zero-length stream writes can panic.\n> - Host panic when component call_async is cancelled under some\n>   conditions.\n> - Panic on erroneous call-to-host from guest realloc call.\n> - Yielding in a component start function can lead to a host panic.\n> - Panic when invoking an async-lifted function via call.\n> - Panic when pending calls are run after a trap.\n> - Stack overflow dropping a long chain of recursive types.\n> - Wasmtime may not properly enforce async-entrypoint requirement.\n> - Panic viewing component model stream or future as the wrong type.\n> - Component-model handle tables are capped only per instance and\n>   charged to no limit.\n> - Exception tags can cause host data structures to be unaligned.\n> - Filesystem sandbox escape when renaming symlinks with trailing\n>   slashes.\n> - Overlapping string transcode in a fused adapter can panic.\n> - Guests can send absolute-form HTTP requests to different hosts.\n> - wasi-http: Request with long url before query parameter crashes\n>   host.\n\n> - wasi-http: Guests can add conflicting content lengths to messages\n> - wasi-http p3: forwarded trailers aren\\'t checked against\n>   is_forbidden_header hook\n> - wasi-http p3: Guests can set incorrect content-length for spliced\n>   response bodies\n> - Cranelift backend on aarch64 can jump to incorrect target on large\n>   Wasm br_table instruction\n> - Panic lowering a host-created component model stream into a guest\n>   that expects a different payload type.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0582",
